<article class="env-definition" id="01CS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01CS">Definition <span data-tag="01CS">17.25.1</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ be a ringed space. An <em>invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module</em> is a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules $\mathcal{L}$ such that the functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O}_ X) \longrightarrow \textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O}_ X),\quad \mathcal{F} \longmapsto \mathcal{L} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{F}  \]
</div>
  <p> is an equivalence of categories. We say that $\mathcal{L}$ is <em>trivial</em> if it is isomorphic as an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module to $\mathcal{O}_ X$. </p>
</article>